DOLLY 7
PACKAGE voxel-flyover
REQUIRES HOST runtime@0
REQUIRES HOST audio@0
REQUIRES HOST display@0
REQUIRES HOST input@0
REQUIRES HOST threads@0
REQUIRES HOST sockets@0
REQUIRES HOST gpu@0
REQUIRES HOST clipboard@0

# Voxel Flyover: a corgi on a jet surfboard flies over an endless world of mountains, forests and
# sea through a day and a night, drawn by Godot's Forward+ renderer on gpu@0. The world is a
# function its shaders compute: a pass draws the ground into textures as the flight goes, and
# the vertex stages raise grids of land to it and stand trees on it. Its
# project (demos/godot/voxel-flyover) is imported and exported here by Godot's editor, and
# voxel-flyover plays the pack with godot, which installs with it. The project installs too.
FROM /v0.1.6/Dollyfile-system 33e5bcf65ef4a634da5dbf8e291a379148e7971aa0411fe1bdaa4e0332f24b94
INSTALL /v0.1.6/demos/godot/Dollyfile-godot f9bfa77355356aa10dae2a7932825a3004f092e8eeb0d3ed333a58211db1a8cb
USE /v0.1.6/demos/godot/Dollyfile-godot-editor 40b356d99d06e3334cca43232df29096f916427434a8c11d684c967ee5b4600b

REQUIRES TOOL cp
REQUIRES TOOL godot-editor
REQUIRES TOOL mkdir
REQUIRES TOOL rm
REQUIRES TOOL tar

SOURCE /v0.1.6/dist/static/godot/voxel-flyover.tar 0a8ba7e1de36d4ffeab5a8ca853974179278cc15cd7397184b2a9d6509b2e54f /tmp/voxel-flyover.tar
SLOP CWD / tar -xf /tmp/voxel-flyover.tar
SLOP mkdir -p /usr/share/voxel-flyover
SLOP cp -r /usr/src/voxel-flyover /usr/share/voxel-flyover/project
SLOP CWD /usr/src/voxel-flyover godot-editor --headless --import
SLOP CWD /usr/src/voxel-flyover godot-editor --headless --export-pack Dolly /usr/share/voxel-flyover/voxel-flyover.pck
SLOP rm -rf /usr/src/voxel-flyover /tmp/voxel-flyover.tar

FILE /usr/bin/voxel-flyover
    #!/bin/slop
    godot --main-pack /usr/share/voxel-flyover/voxel-flyover.pck "$@"
EXPORTS TOOL voxel-flyover
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/voxel-flyover.1
    voxel-flyover [GODOT-OPTION...] [-- --autopilot SECONDS] [-- --day HOUR]
    Plays Voxel Flyover on the page: a corgi in a cape and sunglasses flies a
    jet surfboard over an endless world of mountains, forests and sea, from
    dawn through the day into night, and lights the beacons it reaches, which
    send rings of light over the ground. It flies itself until Enter takes
    the board: arrows or WASD steer, climb and dive, Space is full speed, T
    lets the hours run, Escape lets go of the board, Q quits. With
    --autopilot it flies by itself for that long and prints its
    frame rate, the milliseconds a frame took the GPU and the renderer, the
    beacons it lit and what its frame shows; --day starts at that hour. It
    draws through WebGPU (gpu@0). Its project is
    /usr/share/voxel-flyover/project: copy it to edit it with godot-editor.
FILE /usr/share/voxel-flyover/voxel-flyover.pck
FOLDER /usr/share/voxel-flyover/project
